//ERR 12 12 12 13
//MSG="Break depth has to be positive"

// Leaving zero loops is not a thing the statement can do. The level counts
// loops to unwind, so the smallest meaningful one is 1 — see
// 29_break_one_is_the_default_level.cpl.
//
// This is caught in the parser, not by the depth check that 61e trips, so the
// span is the level on its own rather than the whole statement.

fn main
    for i 0..3
        brk 0
